{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7a1ad318-35e8-4c0e-a1b3-eba09f46f33d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b90e845bce514d36","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-2xr5jmb3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E001.md","content":"# Tutorial packaging format and validation harness\n\n## Description\n\nDefines the tutorial packaging format — metadata, pinned images, and a validation manifest — that makes tutorials versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases, together with the validation harness that checks a packaged tutorial against a release. This format is the contract that the Dashboard tutorial gallery consumes and that tutorial authors package against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Specify the tutorial packaging format: metadata describing the tutorial (identity, journey, form — notebook or pipeline), pinned image references, and a validation manifest declaring the checks a tutorial must pass.\n- Define versioning rules so a tutorial can be updated and re-validated without a Dashboard release.\n- Implement a validation harness that, given a packaged tutorial, executes the checks declared in its validation manifest and reports a pass/fail result usable in automated testing.\n- Provide at least one example package that exercises the format end to end for harness testing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The packaging format is documented and covers metadata, pinned image references, and a validation manifest, with versioning that lets a tutorial evolve independently of Dashboard releases.\n- Given a packaged tutorial, the validation harness executes its validation manifest and reports a deterministic pass/fail result.\n- At least one example package passes the harness against the current release, proving the format and harness end to end.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3** (P1, raised to P0 by priority inheritance — prerequisite of the P0 gallery and P0 tutorial epics): a tutorial packaging format is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30608,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9aebc69bee2da22f","agent_id":"af1941a7a1e42ee90","session_id":"b3cd4aa6-b92e-42f3-af51-1298ed38d266","uuid":"de14cf69-10ac-472e-b8d8-4685dcc8bfe4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:29:42.315Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
