{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a9f8b432eaf21a4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\t## Epic List\n13\t\n14\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n15\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Notebook-form getting-started tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Pipeline-form getting-started tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n20\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Tutorial gallery usage and contribution documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n21\t\n22\t## Dependency DAG\n23\t\n24\t```mermaid\n25\tgraph TD\n26\t    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E002[\"E002 Dashboard gallery\"]\n27\t    E001 --> E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorials\"]\n28\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Pipeline tutorial\"]\n29\t    E002 --> E005[\"E005 Documentation\"]\n30\t    E003 --> E005\n31\t    E004 --> E005\n32\t```\n33\t\n34\t## DAG Justification\n35\t\n36\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n37\t|------|------|-----------|\n38\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (artifact built against) | The gallery's code renders and launches tutorials from the packaging format's metadata and pinned images; it builds against the format E001 defines. |\n39\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact built against) | Notebook tutorials are packaged (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) per the format E001 defines. |\n40\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 (artifact built against) | The pipeline-form tutorial is packaged per the same format. |\n41\t| E001 → E003/E004 ∥ E002 | Rules 14/15 (parallel) | Once the format exists, gallery code and tutorial authoring proceed independently: the gallery is tested against format-conforming packages, and tutorials are validated by their own per-form validation — neither waits on the other. No edge added. |\n42\t| E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation describes the gallery and contribution process as built; it is blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n43\t\n44\t**Shared-surface enforcement division:** validating packaged tutorials is an enforcement deliverable over the tutorial epics' own surfaces, so it is divided per surface rather than extracted as a standalone harness epic: E003 owns notebook-form validation (workbench launch on the pinned image, run to success), E004 owns pipeline-form validation (import and run), and E002 owns gallery-side conformance (launch strictly from packaging metadata). E001 defines only the shared format specification — the single definition of the data structure all three consume, which is why it remains a standalone epic (two epics must never define the same format independently).\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n47\t\n48\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n49\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n50\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Gallery + one-click launch into project. |\n51\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Six curated journeys split by tutorial form (notebook vs. pipeline), a component/team boundary (Rule 1), not a priority split. |\n52\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Format specification epic (per-form validation is carried in E003/E004 scope — see shared-surface enforcement division below). Priority raised P1→P0 by inheritance: it is the prerequisite of the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and P0 tutorials (HLR-2). |\n53\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | `docs-authoring` priority exception: strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1. |\n54\t\n55\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n56\t\n57\t## Health Warnings\n58\t\n59\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs and Affected Components list; epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR wording, and owner teams were taken from the architecture-context owning teams (`rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md` → RHOAI Dashboard, `rhoai-3.0/notebooks.md` → Workbenches, `rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md` → RHOAI Pipelines).\n60\t- **Documentation has no architecture-context file**, so signal 9 (architecture claims) is scored 0 for E005 and its team assignment is inferred.\n61\t- **Tutorial-form allocation assumption**: the strategy names six journeys but not which are notebook-form vs. pipeline-form. The decomposition follows the journey names: \"first pipeline\" is pipeline-form (E004); the other five (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) are notebook-form (E003). If authoring shows a journey is better served as a pipeline, move it between the two tutorial epics — no DAG change is needed since both depend only on the packaging format.\n62\t- **Component mapping note (Step 2)**: E001 (tutorial packaging format) spans several strategy components (it serves notebook- and pipeline-form tutorials and is consumed by the Dashboard gallery). It is assigned the single most-relevant canonical component `Notebooks`: the format governs notebook images and tutorial content infrastructure, and the strategy explicitly wants it versioned independently of Dashboard releases. E003 is also `Notebooks`/Workbenches — the E001/E003 split is a work-product-type boundary (shared format specification vs. content authoring), per Rule 2.\n63\t- No priority inversions detected. No tiered delivery: no external dependency with uncert