nch files exist; critical path length 3 is\n72\tappropriate for an M-sized strategy (M standard: 3-4). No missing\n73\tdata/artifact edges found in epic content: the gallery is explicitly tested\n74\tagainst E001's format-conforming reference package, and tutorial content\n75\treaches the gallery through the packaging format rather than a code\n76\tdependency, so the absence of E003/E004 → E002 edges is the rule-compliant\n77\tshape, not a gap.\n78\t\n79\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n80\tComponent/team tuples are respected: E002 (Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard), E003\n81\tand E001 (Notebooks / Workbenches), E004 (Data Science Pipelines / RHOAI\n82\tPipelines), E005 (Documentation / RHOAI Documentation). E001 and E003 share a\n83\tcomponent/team but are split on the work-product axis (shared format\n84\tspecification vs. content authoring) per Rule 2 — a correct split, not\n85\tduplication: only E001 defines the format; E003/E004 package against it and\n86\tE002 renders from it. No scope duplication across siblings: no two epics\n87\tindependently build the same data structure or surface (the notebook-form and\n88\tpipeline-form tutorials are different content surfaces, not two presentation\n89\tmodes of one surface). The per-surface validation ownership in E003/E004 is\n90\tthe rule-mandated division of a shared-surface enforcement deliverable, not a\n91\tstandalone enforcement-tool epic. No work-product type mixing within a single\n92\tepic.\n93\t\n94\tMinor: E003 authors, packages, and validates five notebook-form tutorials — a\n95\tsingle logical sweep over one surface set that plausibly exceeds the ~2-week\n96\tguideline, but Health Warnings carry no size estimate or conditional re-split\n97\ttrigger for it (the tutorial-form reallocation note is not a size trigger).\n98\tCorrection: record the re-split trigger in Health Warnings. Do not split by\n99\twork type.\n100\t\n101\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n102\tAll five epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (E001:\n103\tdocumented format + reference package; E002: gallery surface and launch\n104\tmechanics; E003/E004: packaged, validated tutorial content; E005: published\n105\tdocumentation). E001 is correctly Implementation, not Investigation: it\n106\tdelivers a specification artifact and does not resolve uncertainty that would\n107\tchange which downstream epics exist. No `gated_by` / `gate_failure_impact`\n108\tfields are set anywhere, and none are needed — there are no Investigation\n109\tepics and no gates.\n110\t\n111\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n112\tAll epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (none carry\n113\t`investigation_signals`); ai-signals files exist for all five epics and their\n114\trationales match the frontmatter values. Calibration against `.context`:\n115\tE001/E003 cite `rhoai-3.0/notebooks.md`, E002 cites `rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`,\n116\tE004 cites `rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md` — all three files exist and\n117\tthe `architecture_claims: 1` scores with cited rationales are grounded. E005's\n118\t`architecture_claims: 0` is justified: no architecture-context file exists for\n119\tthe Documentation component (verified), so there is nothing to corroborate.\n120\tBorderline-but-defensible calls (E003/E004 `existing_foundation: 0` for new\n121\tcontent on a GA foundation; E005 `human_process_gates: -1` for docs technical\n122\treview) each carry explicit rationales. No arithmetic or threshold checks\n123\tperformed — those are pipeline-computed.\n124\t\n125\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n126\tEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from HLR wording.\n127\tRule-mandated ACs are present where applicable: E005 (docs-authoring) has the\n128\ttechnical-review AC (\"technically reviewed against the implemented gallery and\n129\tthe shipped tutorials\"); no replacement epics exist (the gallery is new\n130\tsurface), so rollback/feature-flag ACs do not apply; no konflux-chain epics\n