lt against) | The pipeline-form tutorial is packaged per the same format. |\n42\t| E001 → E003/E004 ∥ E002 | Rules 14/15 (parallel) | Once the format exists, gallery code and tutorial authoring proceed independently: the gallery is tested against format-conforming packages, and tutorials are validated by their own per-form validation — neither waits on the other. No edge added. |\n43\t| E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation describes the gallery, the packaging format, and the contribution process as built; it is blocked by every Implementation epic, including E001 (the packaging format the contribution docs describe). |\n44\t\n45\t**Shared-surface enforcement division:** validating packaged tutorials is an enforcement deliverable over the tutorial epics' own surfaces, so it is divided per surface rather than extracted as a standalone harness epic: E003 owns notebook-form validation (workbench launch on the pinned image, run to success), E004 owns pipeline-form validation (import and run), and E002 owns gallery-side conformance (launch strictly from packaging metadata). E001 defines only the shared format specification — the single definition of the data structure all three consume, which is why it remains a standalone epic (two epics must never define the same format independently).\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n48\t\n49\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n50\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n51\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Gallery + one-click launch into project. |\n52\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Six curated journeys split by tutorial form (notebook vs. pipeline), a component/team boundary (Rule 1), not a priority split. |\n53\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Format specification epic (per-form validation is carried in E003/E004 scope — see shared-surface enforcement division below). Priority raised P1→P0 by inheritance: it is the prerequisite of the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and P0 tutorials (HLR-2). |\n54\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | `docs-authoring` priority exception: strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1. |\n55\t\n56\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n57\t\n58\t## Health Warnings\n59\t\n60\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs and Affected Components list; epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR wording, and owner teams were taken from the architecture-context owning teams (`rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md` → RHOAI Dashboard, `rhoai-3.0/notebooks.md` → Workbenches, `rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md` → RHOAI Pipelines).\n61\t- **Documentation has no architecture-context file**, so signal 9 (architecture claims) is scored 0 for E005 and its team assignment is inferred.\n62\t- **Tutorial-form allocation assumption**: the strategy names six journeys but not which are notebook-form vs. pipeline-form. The decomposition follows the journey names: \"first pipeline\" is pipeline-form (E004); the other five (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) are notebook-form (E003). If authoring shows a journey is better served as a pipeline, move it between the two tutorial epics — no DAG change is needed since both depend only on the packaging format.\n63\t- **Component mapping note (Step 2)**: E001 (tutorial packaging format) spans several strategy components (it serves notebook- and pipeline-form tutorials and is consumed by the Dashboard gallery). It is assigned the single most-relevant canonical component `Notebooks`: the format governs notebook images and tutorial content infrastructure, and the strategy explicitly wants it versioned independently of Dashboard releases. E003 is also `Notebooks`/Workbenches — the E001/E003 split is a work-product-type boundary (shared format specification vs. content authoring), per Rule 2.\n64\t- **E003 size (no split)**: E003 authors, packages, and validates five notebook-form tutorials — a single logical sweep over one surface set that plausibly exceeds the ~2-week guideline (estimated 3–4 weeks of content authoring plus per-tutorial validation against the current release). Not split: all five tutorials share the same work-product type, the same component/team (Notebooks / Workbenches), the same packaging format, and the same per-surface validation approach — splitting them would duplicate the packaging and validation setup per shard and split one content stream across parallel epics on the same team. Re-split trigger: if authoring is not complete within two sprints, or any single tutorial (most likely first RAG app, the least standard journey) needs more than one sprint of iteration to pass its validation manifest, split E003 along journey lines (e.g., core workbench/training/deployment journeys vs. the RAG app tutorial) — each shard keeps the same dependencies (the packaging format) and the same per-surface validation ownership.\n65\t- No priority inversions detected. No tiered delivery: no external dependency with uncertain timing (Open Questions: none; no Dependencies table).\n66\t\n67\t## Tiered Delivery\n68\t\n69\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is in-platform.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8989316470649861","agent_id":"a9bea315f29d46828","session_id":"b3cd4aa6-b92e-42f3-af51-1298ed38d266","uuid":"f9d9f4d2-97e4-4213-887c-21147cf8a6be","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:38:21.339Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a07300c9e4f705ab","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
